flowchart RL
  accTitle: Hypotheses about slow room-booking confirmation
  accDescr: The problem, slow booking confirmation, is on the left. Possible causes are to the right, and each arrow asks Why. Requests have no shared checklist and arrive through several channels, so details are missing. Missing details lead to repeated questions. Calendar updates are done by hand, so availability information conflicts, which also leads to repeated questions. There is no agreed backup approver, so requests wait for one coordinator. Each link is a hypothesis to test. Two notes suggest actions: test a request checklist and compare how often details are missing before and after, and name a backup approver with an agreed time to escalate waiting requests.
  checklist["No shared request checklist"] -->|Why?| details["Missing booking details"]
  channels["Requests split across channels"] -->|Why?| details
  details -->|Why?| clarification["Repeated clarification"]
  clarification -->|Why?| effect["SLOW BOOKING\nCONFIRMATION"]
  cover["No agreed approval cover"] -->|Why?| queue["Requests wait for one coordinator"]
  queue -->|Why?| effect
  manual["Calendar updated manually"] -->|Why?| availability["Conflicting availability information"]
  availability -->|Why?| clarification
  checklistNote@{ shape: comment, label: "Problem-solving<br/>Pilot a request checklist;<br/>compare missing-detail rates<br/>before and after." }
  coverNote@{ shape: comment, label: "Mitigation<br/>Assign a deputy approver<br/>and agree when to escalate<br/>waiting requests." }
  checklistNote -.- checklist
  coverNote -.- cover
  classDef annotation fill:none,color:#002d74,stroke:#005cb9,stroke-width:1px;
  class checklistNote,coverNote annotation;
  classDef effect fill:#002d74,color:#ffffff,stroke:#00a0df,stroke-width:3px;
  class effect effect;
